It's the fall of 1918. The Great War is raging. More than a million American men have found themselves in the Muzargon offensive on the Western Front. It remains, to this day, the deadliest campaign in our military's history, and the conditions were horrendous. So it's rainy, it's muddy, it's freezing, and this is the beginning of trench warfare. These soldiers are hanging out in ditches in the mud. people are dying everywhere. It's miserable.
